// Technology fingerprints.
//
// Every rule is [name, category, signals]. A technology is reported when any one of its signals matches.
//   h  response headers: { 'header-name': RegExp, or true when the header only has to exist }
//   c  cookie names set by the page (RegExp tested against each name)
//   m  <meta name|property|http-equiv> content: { name: RegExp, or true when the tag only has to exist }
//   a  URLs the page loads: scripts, stylesheets and other <link>s, images, frames, media (RegExp)
//   s  URLs of scripts and <link>s only (RegExp). For folder names of a platform: an image or a text link can point at
//      somebody else's website, the scripts and stylesheets of a page are its own.
//   j  inline <script> text (RegExp)
//   x  the HTML source without the text of its scripts (RegExp)
//   u  host name of the final URL (RegExp)
//   g  Google Tag Manager container: built-in tag ids (array) that load this technology
//   i  technologies that this one implies (array of names)
//   r  another technology that must have been found for this one to count (name)
//   n  host names on which the technology is never reported (RegExp)
// When a pattern has capture groups, the first group that matched is reported as the version.

